{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Wavefront OBJ and MTL Format.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Wavefront OBJ and MTL Format.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"wavefront obj and mtl format wavefront obj and mtl format","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Wavefront OBJ and MTL Format.md","fileName":"Wavefront OBJ and MTL Format.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Wavefront OBJ and MTL Format","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Portable 3D Model Data]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Portable 3D Model Data","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Wavefront OBJ and MTL Format.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Wavefront OBJ and MTL Format.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"wavefront obj and mtl format wavefront obj and mtl format","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Wavefront OBJ and MTL Format.md","fileName":"Wavefront OBJ and MTL Format.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Wavefront OBJ and MTL Format","heading":"Wavefront OBJ and MTL Format","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Wavefront OBJ is a human-readable interchange format for mesh geometry. It can declare vertices, texture coordinates, normals, and faces that index those collections. Its companion MTL file describes material-related information referenced by the model.\n\nOBJ's indexed faces can reuse a vertex across several polygons and can represent faces with more than three coplanar points. This makes the format relatively compact and understandable, while its deliberately limited scope also makes it more portable than an application-native project file.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Portable 3D Model Data","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Wavefront OBJ and MTL Format.